{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting the Job You Want", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Practical Advice", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future Continuous Tense vs. The Future Perfect Tense ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"italic\">Future Continuous </span>tense to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future.<br/>You use the<span class=\"italic\"> Future Perfect</span> tense to talk about one action that will happen before another action in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> tense, the action will have started in the future, but it will not be finished. It will be ongoing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will be working</span> at 4 p.m. tomorrow. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The person will  be working in the future, at 4 p.m. When the person will stop working is not stated. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the Future Continuous is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will</span> + <span class=\"italic\">be</span> + verb <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">By this time tomorrow, we <span class=\"strong\">will be getting on</span> a plane heading on our vacation. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With the<span class=\"strong\"> Future Perfect</span> tense we often use a time marker to specify when something will have happened by.<br><br> For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">We can leave until 10 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have picked</span> up the car by then.  <br/>The movie will start at 9 p.m. You will arrive at the theater at 9:15 p.m. When you arrive, the movie <span class=\"strong\">will have started</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the Future Perfect tense is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will </span>+  <span class=\"italic\">have </span>+ past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">By this time tomorrow <span class=\"strong\">we will have finished</span> our project.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you think we will have it finished by 9:00 p.m. tonight?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Will we be working on it all night?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "By this time tomorrow we will have finished our project and we will be getting on a plane heading on our vacation. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Mike will have done all his work by 5:00 p.m.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think we'll have put it to bed before that even. I think we'll have it ready by 6:00, maybe 7:00 ... at the max.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will be doing some research on Corbin. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Tag Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A question tag is a short question at the end of a statement.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These questions are used  to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">clarify/confirm whether what you have said is or is not true</span>. </li><li>They also<span class=\"strong\"> signal the listener that you expect a reply</span> from them.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'yes' <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you?</span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</li></ul></span></li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'no'  <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were you? </span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul></span> </li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same. <br/>For <span class=\"strong\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do</span>/<span class=\"italic\">does </span>or <span class=\"italic\">did</span>/<span class=\"italic\">didn't</span>. <br/>Look at the examples in the chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I think we met at Jack's house, didn't we?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Hey ... I know you, don't I?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We were all at Melrose bar, weren't we?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You work at Corbin Development, don't you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sure, you will be heading this way, won't you? ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Create an elevator pitch with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of a situation when you would need to make an elevator pitch.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An elevator pitch is a brief, persuasive speech that you use to spark interest.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can create interest in a project, idea, product, or in yourself. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A good elevator pitch is 20 to 30 seconds, but make yours 1 minute.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Role play with a partner. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to talk about what you will be doing or what you will have done in your pitch. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you are ready change partners.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I collaborate with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create an elevator pitch dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use will be doing or what I will have done to talk about future plans.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I act out and perform my dialogue.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to overhear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to hear a conversation without the speaker's intention or notice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I couldn't help but overhear your conversation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "put to bed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to complete work on something and send it on to the next step in production", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think we'll have put it to bed before that even.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "max", "type": "name"}, {"content": "maximum", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think we'll have it ready by 6:00, maybe 7:00 \u2026 at the max.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "proposal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of proposing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are finishing up a development proposal for the city planners. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "neck of the woods", "type": "name"}, {"content": "area of the country ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What are you doing in this neck of the woods? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to head", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move in the direction of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will be heading this way, won't you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about emotions, opinions and behavior in a work situation. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can ask for clarification and ask for someone's opinion. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Are you good at starting conversations with strangers? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What techniques do you use?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feed